meta {
  name: 21-Ask a question publicly on the listing
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/api/listings/1/comments
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{temi_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "body": "Hi! Is the ₦850k figure for one year or two? And does the caution fee come back when I move out, or is it gone? First-time renter, sorry for the basics."
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: in [201, 401, 404]
}

docs {
  I'm asking the question that anyone moving out of their parents'
  house in Lagos has — is the rent for one year or two, and does
  the caution fee come back? I'd much rather ask publicly so the
  next first-timer sees the answer.

  As a Lagos renter the platform itself should already explain
  caution fee in tooltips. Asking it in comments is a workaround.
}
